        "explanation": "Correct. The systolic signal does not begin with the onset of QRS, which is typical of MR or TR. Hence this is indicative of aortic stenosis (AS) with aortic regurgitation (AR). The AS signal is midpeaking, which correlates with a slow rise in aortic pressure, as the kinetic energy associated with the jet is very significant and this results in a corresponding drop in potential energy. Note that the end of the AS signal is con- tinuous with the AR signal and vice versa. This indicates the origin of the signals at the same valve."
